# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Environment variables — NEVER commit real credentials.
# `*.local` above already catches .env.local, but be explicit: a leaked
# Supabase service_role key gives full read/write access to every table,
# bypassing Row Level Security.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Supabase CLI working files. The `supabase/` folder itself IS committed —
# migrations and config.toml are your version-controlled schema — but these
# machine-specific subfolders are not.
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/

# Test & coverage output
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Shared VS Code workspace settings are committed so the team stays consistent.
!.vscode/settings.json

# Playwright MCP scratch output (page snapshots taken during verification)
.playwright-mcp/

# MCP server configuration. Ignored because it is the natural place for someone
# to paste a Supabase personal access token, and that token grants management
# access to every project the account can see. The committed template is
# .mcp.json.example; the real file stays on each machine.
.mcp.json

# ============================================================================
# OPERATIONAL SCRIPTS AND WORKING NOTES
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are for running THIS deployment, not for anybody who clones the repo.
#
# The two SQL files empty the database, including every user account. They are
# written to be pasted into the Supabase SQL editor by somebody who has read
# them first. In a public repository they are an instruction manual for
# destroying the system, sitting next to the project ref that names it.
#
# BUILD-PLAN.md is a development log — decisions, dead ends and the mistakes
# made along the way. Useful to whoever is building; not part of the product.
#
# The handover docs (GOING-LIVE, AUTH-SETUP, WALKTHROUGH, PAYMENTS) ARE
# committed on purpose: they are how somebody else runs this after you.
# ============================================================================
supabase/clear-demo-data.sql
supabase/reset-to-production.sql
docs/BUILD-PLAN.md

# Local scratch
scripts/clean-probes.mjs
